coder › Implemented `deepMerge(base, over)` in `src/merge.ts` and added tests in `src/merge.test.ts`.

What changed
- `src/merge.ts`
  - Merges plain objects key by key recursively (a value is "plain" when its prototype is `Object.prototype` or `null` and it is not an array).
  - Arrays and any other non-plain value in `over` replace `base`'s value.
  - `undefined` in `over` leaves `base`'s value untouched; `null` replaces it.
  - `__proto__`, `constructor`, and `prototype` keys in `over` are ignored.
  - Neither argument is mutated; arrays and plain objects on both sides are deep-cloned so the result shares no object with either input.
  - All result keys are written with `Object.defineProperty`, so a base key named `__proto__` becomes a safe own data property instead of triggering the prototype setter.

- `src/merge.test.ts`
  - Kept the existing flat-merge test and added coverage for: recursive merge, array/`null`/other-value replacement, `undefined` leaving base alone, `null` replacing, no mutation of inputs, no shared references, ignored dangerous keys in `over`, and a JSON document with a `__proto__` key polluting nothing.

